# Technical Decisions

Some choices will affect the quality of the predictions and how reliably the results can be reproduced. I'll record the reasoning here as those choices are made.

| Topic | What needs to be decided | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Data cleaning | How to handle missing or invalid records | To investigate |
| Train/test split | Which time periods to use for evaluation | To investigate |
| Baseline | Which simple method to compare against | To investigate |
| Evaluation | Which metrics to report | To investigate |
| Reproducibility | How to record dependencies and run settings | To investigate |

## Recording a decision

For important choices, I'll note the alternatives considered, why one approach was selected, and how it was checked. Decisions may be updated if the data or experiment results suggest a better approach.
